{
  "borough": "Sutton",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The applicant has failed to provide adequate marketing evidence to demonstrate that the loss of the Class E commercial floor space is justified or that the unit is surplus to requirements. The proposed change of use is therefore contrary to Local Plan Policy 16.",
    "The scale, massing, and design of the proposed mansard roof extension and over-proliferation of side dormer windows would be overly dominant and visually intrusive on this corner plot, failing to respect the character of the adjacent terrace which is set back. The development is considered to result in poor design, contrary to London Plan Policy D4 and Local Plan Policy 28.",
    "The application fails to provide the necessary technical supporting information, specifically an Energy Statement and Part G water efficiency calculations. Without this documentation, the proposal is unable to demonstrate compliance with the mandatory requirements for achieving a 35% reduction in CO2 emissions and a 10% reduction from renewables (Local Plan Policy 31), or the confirmation of water efficiency targets (Local Plan Policy 33). The proposal is therefore contrary to London Plan Policies SI 2 and SI 5 and Local Plan Policies 31 and 33."
  ],
